00:06:50.870 --> 00:06:52.510
They don't get any support.

00:06:52.510 --> 00:06:56.930
So if you have a website on it for your
company and you are making money, just

00:06:56.930 --> 00:06:59.190
make sure that you have a good developer.

00:06:59.190 --> 00:07:02.430
And don't be cheap and go to a one-dollar
hosting.

00:07:02.430 --> 00:07:04.390
OK, last big question.

00:07:04.390 --> 00:07:05.750
What can we do?

00:07:05.750 --> 00:07:07.550
I would say rely on the big companies.

00:07:07.550 --> 00:07:12.190
Make sure it's working through Cloudflare
with a firewall in front of it and a DDoS

00:07:12.190 --> 00:07:16.350
protection. Use SSH keys.

00:07:16.350 --> 00:07:19.430
Don't use passwords. That's so stupid.

00:07:19.430 --> 00:07:24.230
Rotate your SSH keys every few months.

00:07:24.230 --> 00:07:28.910
And API keys: don't set them to infinite
use.

00:07:28.910 --> 00:07:31.030
Keep rotating those too.

00:07:31.030 --> 00:07:35.060
And make sure you update and don't push
your

00:07:35.060 --> 00:07:37.310
.env file to GitHub.

00:07:37.310 --> 00:07:40.195
Okay. I did both of those actions.

00:07:40.195 --> 00:07:45.480
I did that once. Opus 4.8 was not that
smart.

00:07:45.480 --> 00:07:50.630
And I did the migration from closed to
